{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11620 - MONDO_8159",
  "verbalization": "Neridronic Acid is linked to Postmenopausal Osteoporosis through a chain of indications that involve the treatment of osteoporosis. The evidence suggests that Neridronic Acid is used to treat Humoral Hypercalcemia of Malignancy, which in turn is linked to Incadronic Acid and Minodronic Acid, both of which are indicated for Postmenopausal Osteoporosis. This indicates a potential pathway where Neridronic Acid may exert a therapeutic effect through a mechanism that involves calcium regulation or bone metabolism, possibly through a similar mechanism to other bisphosphonates. The overlapping indications suggest a possible shared therapeutic target or mechanism of action across these drugs. The evidence supports a relationship between Neridronic Acid and Postmenopausal Osteoporosis, though the exact mechanism remains unclear, and further research is needed to clarify the precise role of Neridronic Acid in this context.",
